# N5c: TIMED arm A (the control, the speed twin, with hang fix QWEN_FAST_REQUEST_SHARD_ARGMAX) of the paired timing ABAB on coding prompts (audits OFF). Arms alternate A B A B in this one image, each after its own
# all-four reset, same admission order: A = c2-packed-tp4-speed-rshard (the control), B = c2-packed-tp4-best-rshard (the levers). Second of two A runs.
# c2-packed-tp4-best-rshard is c2-packed-tp4-speed-rshard plus the quad draft, the fused commit in place on live banks and the five verify-glue
# levers, nothing else (test_c2_packed_tp4_profiles); each arm is its base plus QWEN_FAST_REQUEST_SHARD_ARGMAX=1 alone, so the levers are the ONLY difference between the arms and both carry the tail caps.
# The tests: warmup, coding (one stream), concurrent4_code_equal (four real-code prompts of 4k, the padded-4k shape) and
# concurrent4_code_32k (four real-code prompts of 32k, the long-context shape). 800 tokens out each, started together.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/next-2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed
# from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image N0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-2 is a PLACEHOLDER: the driver of the window may substitute it (in every template) once the image is built
# from the pushed branch; the driver's IMAGE_TAG env overrides it.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; engine build 10-20 min on a warm cache (30 min the first time a profile compiles); the four tests
# 15-35 min (the 32k prefill queue dominates): 30-60 min.
# Read: the [PACKED-PHASE] lines (verify: input, trace, sync, readback; commits; early draft; gap) and [PACKED-PUBLISH] medians at 4
# live in each concurrent test: the round wall, commits (eager arms about 38 ms; fused arms about 2 ms), the per-user decode_tok_s
# and the [ACCEPT] mean. Judge the arms PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians; check the load average around the run (a busy
# host skews host phases 10-20%) and repeat before believing a small gap. Then offline: python scripts/ci/speed_window_compare.py
# <A results> <B results> --users 0,1,2,3 --position-keyed --strict-concurrent-prefixes (exit 0 identical, 1 a different draft, 2 too few
# shared positions): the levers are byte-identical replacements, so every user's text and accepted-prefix sequence must be IDENTICAL
# between A and B, and B's 4k texts must equal N1's audited ones.
# OPTIONAL: the numbers are the product. Every timed audits-off arm carries a hang fix: without one S2 deadlocks (tp4-serve-6, S0t). Hang fix B, QWEN_FAST_REQUEST_SHARD_ARGMAX=1, is unproven on hardware: run this pair only if R1..R1e all completed (a stall there skips it). The strace pair is N4a-N4d.
# a HANG on a timed arm is a finding, and the control carries the same hang fix.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-2
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-rshard
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent4_code_32k
